        "start_line": 1,
        "end_line": 4
      },
      "excerpt": "Title:\nEmpty tensor with dtype float16 converted from numpy causes segmentation fault in torch.mul and torch.div\n\n",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": "@AmazingCreator-lmx",
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:4959ea8c32b4fd833c9807f632a0ed6531c81e685db60661bc4425eea197c155"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_expected_behavior_0ef58c1d2773",
      "source_artifact_ref": "art_primary_report",
      "evidence_kind": "expected_behavior",
      "locator": {
        "locator_type": "line_range",
        "start_line": 59,
        "end_line": 84
      },
      "excerpt": "Expected behavior:\n\ntorch.mul should correctly handle multiplication involving empty tensors.\n\nThe operation should either:\n- return a valid empty tensor result\n- or raise an explicit runtime error\n\nIt should not crash the process.\n\n\nMinimal Reproducer:\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport torch\n\na = torch.tensor([2], dtype=torch.float16)\n\nb = torch.tensor(\n    np.array([], dtype='float16')\n)\n\nresult = torch.mul(a, b)\n\n\n",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": "@AmazingCreator-lmx",
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
      "content_hash": "sha256:94fb9d9e073aab329bb3ebaebff206c0f5427543ab37122f4ee7ee6109162770"
    },
    {
      "evidence_id": "ev_art_primary_report_source_metadata_1041ccf1af5e",
