        "start_line": 85,
        "end_line": 163
      },
      "excerpt": "Environment:\n\nPyTorch version:\n2.1.1+cpu\n\n\nPython version:\n3.10.9\n\n\nOS:\nUbuntu 20.04.5 LTS\n\n\nCUDA available:\nFalse\n\n\nDevice:\nCPU\n\n\nCompiler:\nGCC 9.4.0\n\n\nCMake:\n3.16.3\n\n\nRelevant libraries:\n\nnumpy==1.26.2\n\ntorch==2.1.1+cpu\n\ntorchvision==0.16.1+cpu\n\n\nRoot cause information:\n\nThe issue report does not provide detailed root cause analysis.\n\nThe problem appears related to incorrect handling of empty float16 tensors in CPU element-wise operations.\n\n\nFix information:\n\nThe issue was fixed in a later PyTorch version.\n\nA contributor reported:\n\n\"Fixed in latest torch.\"\n\n\nPull Request:\n\n#115183\n\n\nImpact:\n\nThis is a correctness and stability issue.\n\nAn invalid tensor input can cause a hard crash instead of returning an error.\n\nThe failure affects programs using:\n- empty tensors\n- float16 dtype\n- element-wise operators such as torch.mul\n\n\nRelated operators:\n\ntorch.mul\n\ntorch.div\n\n",
      "attribution": {
        "actor": "@AmazingCreator-lmx",
        "actor_role": "reporter"
      },
